      <div class="grid g-2 mt-14" style="grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)"><article class="scard lift reveal" style="transition-delay:0ms"><div class="pic img-zoom"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/7391720/pexels-photo-7391720.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&dpr=2&w=1600" alt="Riad lounge with carved plaster and lantern light" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="txt"><span class="kicker">Marrakech</span><h3>Royal Mansour Marrakech</h3><p>A city of private riads inside the walls — commissioned for heads of state, now yours for a week.</p></div></article><article class="scard lift reveal" style="transition-delay:80ms"><div class="pic img-zoom"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/27945049/pexels-photo-27945049.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&dpr=2&w=1600" alt="Palace courtyard with fountain and arches" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="txt"><span class="kicker">Marrakech</span><h3>La Mamounia</h3><p>The legendary palace garden. Churchill painted here. You will understand why by the second breakfast.</p></div></article><article class="scard lift reveal" style="transition-delay:160ms"><div class="pic img-zoom"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/37441764/pexels-photo-37441764.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&dpr=2&w=1600" alt="Palm oasis and kasbah walls" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="txt"><span class="kicker">Skoura</span><h3>Dar Ahlam</h3><p>A kasbah with no menu and no itinerary. They invent the day around you.</p></div></article><article class="scard lift reveal" style="transition-delay:240ms"><div class="pic img-zoom"><img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/10434667/pexels-photo-10434667.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&dpr=2&w=1800" alt="Private desert camp in the Sahara" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div><div class="txt"><span class="kicker">Sahara</span><h3>Merzouga private camps</h3><p>Canvas, brass, and a bed that faces the erg. Luxury that knows when to stay quiet.</p></div></article></div>
