<section class="sec bg-ivory" id="faq">
  <div class="container cols c-4-8 items-start">
    <div class="reveal"><p class="eyebrow">Questions, answered</p><h2 class="h2 big">What American travelers <span class="it">usually ask first.</span></h2><p class="lead">If it is not here, <a class="link" href="{{ route('faq') }}">read every answer <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></p></div>
    <div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item open reveal" style="transition-delay:0ms"><button type="button" class="faq-q" aria-expanded="true">Is Morocco actually a luxury destination — or is that marketing?<span class="tog" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div><p>It is both, which is why the operator matters. The same medina can feel like a gift or a gauntlet. We work the former: private houses, timed entries, drivers who know the back gates, and camps that are genuinely quiet. Luxury here is access and editing, not marble for its own sake.</p></div></div></div><div class="faq-item reveal" style="transition-delay:40ms"><button type="button" class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How do we get there from the United States?<span class="tog" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div><p>Most of our guests fly nonstop to Casablanca (CMN) from New York, Washington, or Boston, then a short hop to Marrakech — or connect via Madrid, Lisbon, Paris, or London into RAK. We design the landing: meet-and-greet, lounge if useful, and a car that is already waiting. West Coast guests often break in Europe; we will say so if it is kinder.</p></div></div></div><div class="faq-item reveal" style="transition-delay:80ms"><button type="button" class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">When should we go?<span class="tog" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div><p>March through May and late September through November are the country’s most flattering months — clear light, kind evenings, the desert still sleeping well. Summer is possible on the coast and in the High Atlas. December to February is beautiful in the south and crisp in Fès. We will be honest if your dates fight the weather.</p></div></div></div><div class="faq-item reveal" style="transition-delay:120ms"><button type="button" class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is it safe? Can we drink the water? What about solo women?<span class="tog" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div><p>Guests from our cities travel here constantly — couples, families, women on their own. We use known drivers, tracked cars, and hotels we would send our own families to. Drink bottled water; we stock the car. Dress is relaxed in Marrakech and the desert, a little more covered in Fès and the north. We brief you once, then we let you enjoy the place.</p></div></div></div><div class="faq-item reveal" style="transition-delay:160ms"><button type="button" class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Do you only do private travel?<span class="tog" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div><p>Yes for guests. We do not run group departures. We also work as a local DMC for a small number of agencies and design weddings, retreats, and corporate gatherings. The standard is the same: one country, handled quietly.</p></div></div></div><div class="faq-item reveal" style="transition-delay:200ms"><button type="button" class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What is actually included — and what isn’t?<span class="tog" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div><p>Every proposal is itemized. Typically: stays, private transport, guiding, listed meals, experiences, and concierge. International flights, travel insurance, personal shopping, and some extraordinary requests sit outside. If a number is soft, we say so. If a door might not open, we do not sell it.</p></div></div></div><div class="faq-item reveal" style="transition-delay:240ms"><button type="button" class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How far in advance should we plan?<span class="tog" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div><p>For Royal Mansour, La Mamounia, Dar Ahlam, and the better Sahara camps, four to six months is civilized — eight if you are traveling over the holidays or with a group. We have built beautiful journeys in three weeks. We would rather tell you what is no longer possible than pretend.</p></div></div></div><div class="faq-item reveal" style="transition-delay:280ms"><button type="button" class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can you work with our travel advisor?<span class="tog" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button><div class="faq-a"><div><p>Gladly. Many of our American guests come through advisors. We are a local atelier and a reliable DMC: we design, we hold, we execute. Your advisor remains your relationship. We remain the ground.</p></div></div></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

